            {"page_number": 9, "operation": "CREATE", "text": "Near the end of term, Heroic Heights faced a real problem. A section of the school's foundations had developed a crack that the structural engineer said was serious. The students were given the challenge for real: solve this problem before the affected wing had to close. Teams formed — strength teams to shore up walls, speed teams to evacuate equipment, intelligence teams to model solutions. Nadia was given team leadership, which surprised her. She sat everyone down and spent twenty minutes just asking questions before she let anyone do anything. When they finally acted, they acted correctly, and the problem took four hours instead of the estimated two days."},
            {"page_number": 10, "operation": "CREATE", "text": "On the last day of term, capes were reassessed. One by one, students went to the front and their capes shimmered into whatever they had become. Theo's deepened red. Suki's blazed blue. Reed's shone gold. When Nadia stood at the front, her cape blazed so brilliantly silver that students shielded their eyes. It was not a colour she had seen on any cape before. 'Silver and grey,' said Ms Marvel quietly, 'make platinum.' She held up the assembly register. On the first page, in the column for most valuable students: Nadia's name, at the top, with a star. Not because she was the strongest or the fastest or the cleverest. Because she helped everyone else be better. THE END"},
